1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:06,930
Slide 27 introduces "THE SECURITY MATRIX: PROTECTING THE DIGITAL AVATAR."

2
00:00:07,830 --> 00:00:18,955
Giving an autonomous avatar sovereign access to your email, file storage, payment gateways, and cloud infrastructure introduces unprecedented security challenges.

3
00:00:18,955 --> 00:00:29,120
How do we prevent prompt injection attacks, unauthorized spending, and runaway recursive loops from compromising our identity and enterprise assets?

4
00:00:30,020 --> 00:00:41,610
In Part 4, we examine the security matrix through the lens of zero-trust architecture: AP2 payment escrow, SHA-256 cryptographic audit trails, and kernel-level sandbox defense-in-depth.

5
00:00:42,510 --> 00:00:51,440
We will analyze threat models ranging from indirect document injection in untrusted PDFs to malicious API spoofing and session hijacking.

6
00:00:52,340 --> 00:01:02,400
We will demonstrate how to implement sandboxed execution environments using isolated Docker containers, read-only file systems, and restrictive AppArmor security profiles.

7
00:01:03,300 --> 00:01:10,894
An architect who designs powerful autonomous tools without strict security guardrails is building on sand.

8
00:01:10,894 --> 00:01:18,130
Let us begin by analyzing the catastrophic financial risks of uncontrolled agent wallets on Slide 28.

